<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Hejaz and Nejd</h1><p class="st-meta">1926 CE – 1932 CE · capital Riyadh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dual kingdom of Ibn Saud, uniting the holy cities with Najd, and the immediate forerunner of Saudi Arabia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After conquering the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Kingdom of Hejaz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a> was proclaimed King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in January 1926 while remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a>. In 1927 Nejd was also raised to a kingdom, and the two realms were ruled in personal union.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Hejaz</a> kept its own administration and consultative council under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud's</a> son Faisal as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> was ruled directly. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jeddah-1927">Treaty of Jeddah</a> in 1927 brought British recognition of full independence. The Ikhwan, angry at modern innovations and limits on raiding, rebelled; Ibn Saud defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sabilla">Battle of Sabilla</a> in 1929 and crushed the revolt by 1930.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 23 September 1932 a royal decree unified the dual kingdom as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saudi-arabia">Kingdom of Saudi Arabia</a>, named after the ruling family.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-hejaz-and-nejd.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Hejaz and Nejd" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: The Shura Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt>